WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.795 --> 00:00:06.649
Hi! This video shows how to download Claude Blocks, and how to make your first project.

2
00:00:07.316 --> 00:00:12.783
First, go to the Claude Blocks website. It shows the best download for your device.

3
00:00:13.475 --> 00:00:22.181
Scroll down to see every version: Mac, Windows, Linux, and Android and Chromebook. On an iPhone or iPad, use the web version.

4
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:31.981
Download the file and open it. The first time on a Mac, right-click Claude Blocks and choose Open. On Windows, click More info, then Run anyway.

5
00:00:34.241 --> 00:00:40.965
Now open Claude Blocks. The blocks are on the left, your workspace is in the middle, and the stage is on the right.

6
00:00:41.618 --> 00:00:46.037
Let's start fresh. Click New, then choose Blank project.

7
00:00:46.714 --> 00:00:53.997
Open Events, and drag the when green flag clicked block into the workspace. Every script starts with a hat block like this.

8
00:00:54.635 --> 00:00:57.859
From Looks, snap a say block underneath.

9
00:00:58.521 --> 00:01:08.634
From Control, add a forever loop. Then put move ten steps, and if on edge, bounce, inside it.

10
00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:13.670
Click Go! Claude says hello, then walks back and forth.

11
00:01:14.321 --> 00:01:20.954
Want ideas? Click Templates and pick one, like Catch the Apple.

12
00:01:21.593 --> 00:01:29.597
Press Go, then move your mouse to catch the apples!

13
00:01:30.262 --> 00:01:37.534
Click Learn for step by step lessons. A guide stays on screen while you build.

14
00:01:38.226 --> 00:02:08.716
Stuck? In the AI Assistant, choose Build for me, describe what you want, and the AI makes the blocks for you. It uses Ollama on your computer.

15
00:02:09.739 --> 00:02:15.873
Check the plan, then click Add and run. Your new blocks appear in the workspace, ready to change.

16
00:02:16.596 --> 00:02:28.511
Claude Blocks even has a Raspberry Pi emulator, with lights, a fan, a screen and more. This thermostat turns the fan on when the chip gets hot.

17
00:02:29.194 --> 00:02:33.672
When you're done, click Save to keep your project. Have fun coding!

